From fb9aa2721472534092f737612550a0d8e157c291 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ruben van der Linde <ruben@conduction.nl>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:00:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(learniq): keep the certificate PDF from widening the
 credential units [skip ci]

The PDF render added a seventh constructor parameter to the issuance
handler and the reissue service and a course parameter to the reissue
steps, which lowered the unit interfacing rating (3.62 -> 3.60).

- CredentialDocuments holds the Europass issuer and the PDF renderer, so
  both constructors keep six parameters.
- The reissue run carries the course, read once per run as before; the
  PDF step returns only the fields it writes.
- payload() reads the template slug from the course; the render outcome
  is written by rendered() / notRendered().

Same calls, same order, same stored fields. Rating back to 3.62.

Assisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5
